      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Michael Boland is delighted to present this beautifully maintained three-bedroom semi-detached residence, ideally positioned in the heart of the picturesque village of Lahardane, Co. Mayo.\n\nPresented in exceptional show-house condition throughout, this attractive home offers a superb turnkey opportunity for any purchaser seeking a property that is ready for immediate occupation. Bright, spacious and thoughtfully laid out, the accommodation is finished to a high standard and offers an excellent balance of comfortable living space and practical family accommodation.\n\nOriginally constructed as a four-bedroom residence, the property has since been reconfigured to provide three generous bedrooms, allowing for a more spacious and versatile internal layout. One of the bedrooms is conveniently located on the ground floor, making the property particularly suitable for a wide range of buyers, including families, downsizers, retirees or those requiring flexible guest or home-office accommodation.\n\nThe living areas are well proportioned and enjoy an abundance of natural light, while the overall presentation reflects the care and attention the current owners have given to the property. The home has been maintained to an excellent standard throughout and offers the benefit of modern, comfortable living without the need for any immediate refurbishment.\n\nA particularly attractive feature of the property is its setting overlooking the Titanic Memorial Garden, one of Lahardane's most recognised and historic landmarks. This unique outlook adds great character to the home and enhances its strong village setting.\n\nLahardane is a charming and well-established North Mayo village, surrounded by scenic countryside and offering a strong sense of community. The property is conveniently located close to local amenities and services, while also providing easy access to surrounding towns and villages.\n\nWith its excellent condition, flexible three-bedroom layout, ground-floor bedroom, central village location and attractive outlook, F26 A3F9 represents an excellent opportunity to acquire a beautifully presented home in a highly appealing setting.\n\nThis property is sure to attract interest from first-time buyers, families, those looking to downsize, investors or purchasers seeking a turnkey home in the heart of rural Mayo."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 1.98m x 6390m\nPorch with ornate tiles- coving understairs\n\nLiving Room - 3.52m x 4.04m\nInsert Stove, built in carpentry, coving\n\nKitchen/ Dining Room - 3.57m x 8.11m\nTiled floor, coving, recessed lighting, quality kitchen with granite stone work tops. Isnald with oak work tops.\n\nConservatory - 4.74m x 3.45m\nValuted ceiling, slider patio door to garden area, quallity floring , oak double doors\n\nShower Room - 2.71m x 1.95m\nTiled Floors, fully tiled bathroom, ornate quality tiles, upgraded sanitary ware, double shower with Mira electric shower.\n\nMaster Bedroom - 4.64m x 4.03m\n\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - 1.79m x 2.07m\nDouble Shower, qulaity vanity ware, steam proof mirroe, fully tiled.\n\nWalk in Wardrobe - 1.85m x 1.4m\n\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.42m x 3.6m\n\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - 1.45m x 2m\nFully tile vanity, fully tile dbathroom, pumped shower\n\nWalk in Wardrobe - 1.34m x 1.5m\n\n\nBedroom 3- Ground Floor - 3.57m x 4.05m\n\n\nLanding - 0.93m x 2.70m\n\n\n"
